  "description": "Micheletti's 1998 dissertation protocol as reported by Siever, p. 9: 10-Hz audiovisual stimulation for 2 min, the same auditory stimulus alone for 1 min, then 18-Hz audiovisual stimulation for 2 min; repeated four times (20 min). Lights flash only during the audiovisual phases and stay dark in the auditory-alone minute. Duty, luminance, color, and phase were unreported; neutral defaults: 220-Hz carrier, 50 percent duty, moderate brightness, ears and eyes in phase. Not a treatment recommendation.",
